-import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.ts"
-
-export const twoRouterAppsHoldNoTsconfigSoNothingCompilesTheirRoutes = {
-  id: "01a06936-6faa-78c4-888f-264bcdc57829",
-  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
-  slug: "two-router-apps-hold-no-tsconfig-so-nothing-compiles-their-routes",
-  domainSlug: "domain/akasha-check",
-  claim:
-    "The `typecheck` code-check leaves a router app's routes folder and its root route to the app's own compile, and states that as a `gap` invariant. For five of the seven router apps that promise is kept. `akasha/alan/atlas-web` and `akasha/alan/web-capacitor` hold no `tsconfig.json` at all, so nothing compiles their routes or their root route: not this check, which excludes them, and not the app, which has no compile to run. The `router-app` page type already states the constraint they break.",
-  evidence:
-    "Measured 2026-09-03, after landing e7a1120a43.\n\nSeven pages carry `pageTypeSlug: \"router-app\"`. Testing each folder for `tsconfig.json`: `alan/web`, `audhdalan/audhdalan-web`, `smilingjenny/smilingjenny-web`, `archive-of-worlds/archive-of-worlds-web` and `temper/temper-web` each hold one stating `rootDirs`. `alan/atlas-web` and `alan/web-capacitor` hold none.\n\n`router-app.page-type.ts` states the constraint `The tsconfig naming a fixed name is what gives that name the package's path mappings.` A router app with no tsconfig keeps neither that constraint nor the typecheck's `gap`.\n\nWHAT THIS COST. `akasha/alan/atlas-web/root.tsx` was one of the five root routes refusing `TS2307 Cannot find module './+types/root'` before e7a1120a43. For the other four the refusal was noise, since each app's own compile resolves the specifier through its `rootDirs` and reports nothing; `alan/web/root.tsx` draws 0 TS2307 in a 358-file program parsed from its own tsconfig. For atlas-web there is no such compile, so what the exclusion removed was the only reading anything had of that file. `alan/web-capacitor/root.tsx` was judged and clean before the change and is now unjudged as well, though it imports no generated types and so never refused.\n\nThe routes folders of both apps were already excluded by the rule that stood before this change, so their route files have had no compile for as long as that rule has held. What is new is the root route, and what is worth Alan's eye is that the check's `gap` reads as a promise that something else looks, which for these two apps is not true.\n\nNOT MEASURED. I did not establish why the two apps lack a tsconfig, whether they are built at all, or whether `web-capacitor` compiles through `alan/web` rather than on its own. Giving them a tsconfig is the obvious repair and I did not attempt it, because I have not read what either app builds and a wrong one would read as coverage that is not there.",
-} as const satisfies Finding
